{
  "comment": "Why: a flooded crypt has three kinds of tenant: the drowned (the dead the water kept, the undead tag's drowned), what lives in the water now (the aquatic tag: lizardfolk and the things of the deep), and the dead who were never drowned (skeletons in the dry vaults), plus a siren-like voice (the witch) that leads people to the water. The table is slow, wet and numerous: the packs are drowned (cost one each) and the pressure comes from not being able to see the water move, so two entries need the dark and one needs noise (a bell that wakes the congregation). The roll bonus is plus two as on the plain Abyssal road: the crypt is dark and wet, and the party's torch is the only warm thing in it. The budget scale is 1.1: the drowned are slow, and the air is the real enemy.",
